  "published": "2026-08-25T21:48:10.87Z",
  "releaseNotes": "TCMProject.Utilities: adds PermissionCatalog, which answers which service a permission belongs to. The information already lived in the enum - a permission declares its module with [Parent] and the module declares its service the same way - but only the enum generator read it, so any per-service filter had to be a StartsWith on the name. That breaks the day a permission does not follow the prefix convention. Lets each service receive only its own bits instead of every service carrying every other service permissions in its bitmask. FilterByService deliberately KEEPS permissions that declare no service: filtering is an optimisation, not an access control, and dropping one would turn an incomplete presentation attribute into an authorisation bug. All 50 current permissions resolve to a service (SCHEDULE 17, HEALTH_RECORD 15, PLATFORM 18). Additive; nothing changes for callers that do not filter.",
